      "writtenOn": "2021-02-12T12:05:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Currently there isn\u0027t any asynchronous way of getting this. As JobScheduler always calls the synchronous methods, so the asynchronous way of getting it wasn\u0027t necessary right now. I can add the callback as you suggested but there won\u0027t be any client using it for now, unless we update JobScheduler to start using the asynchronous callbacks which sounds like something we need to do.",
